{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"61b9d00869e292b3b2db63eb675cab0b561c986aca572b9fe9eaa48dbda30f96","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_4d41e7d61729fcfbe0eef9874d91402fcc1f37a6e82490e1ce8ceaeedf486c82","overall_assessment":"The paper is generally well-organized and clearly written, with a logical flow from motivation to method and experiments. The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined, and the algorithmic presentation is clear. The main clarity weakness is a minor typo in the implementation section that could cause confusion for readers attempting to reproduce the results.","paper_id":"BkIqod5ll","paper_identity_sha256":"d129755e29c5adfcbc679d29011381de6975b666de82e7e3579be72a8be34a4b","prompt_identity_sha256":"b395b596dcbecd35405401d2723a67c350805603c3a2e26345b43946aa0a9ba5","raw_response_sha256":"b96e5d4c73f62df4ccf3320071f28eaeee41159d89b8a5e32a6f9a4d492f6a6c","request_identity_sha256":"82fe6993c185454e1c67cdd71403bfa7bc3636587e73b2552cb8005560468278","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"6c3590d1447a48c304ffdda6559d30babd11b5189ab56dea457273eae566f669","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-020"],"review_text":"The paper is well-structured with a clear narrative flow from the introduction of the problem to the proposed method and experimental validation. The terminology is precise, and key concepts such as the transition matrix, expected number of visits, and graph convolution are clearly defined. The algorithm presentation in Section 3.4 is detailed and provides a clear mapping of the tensor operations, which aids in understanding the implementation. However, there is a minor typo in the output dimension description in Section 3.4 where 'Features' is misspelled as 'Feetures'. This should be corrected to avoid confusion for readers.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-010","SRC-011","SRC-012","SRC-014","SRC-016","SRC-018"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined throughout the paper. The definitions of the graph, transition matrix, and expected number of visits are clear and logically connected. The equations for the convolution operations (Conv1 and Conv2) are well-explained, and the notation for the permutation order and the weights is consistent. The derivation of the expected number of visits and its use in selecting neighbors is clearly presented. The notation for the tensor operations in the implementation section is also clear, although the typo in the output dimension should be corrected.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-004","SRC-017","SRC-021","SRC-024","SRC-028"],"review_text":"The figure and table captions are detailed and provide sufficient context for the reader to understand the visual and tabular data. Figure 1 and Figure 2 captions clearly describe the visualization of the graph convolution and the row of the expected number of visits matrix, respectively. Figure 3 caption explains the correlation matrix and the convergence plot. Table 1 and Table 2 are well-structured and provide clear comparisons of the proposed method with other approaches. The textual descriptions of the figures and tables are consistent with the content presented in the paper.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"389ffa3faf8719366b8d0e4dfbfb7a5be6a85d9e51ad53a5f3f34f3101ccb719","paper_id":"BkIqod5ll","paper_ordinal":48,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"b96e5d4c73f62df4ccf3320071f28eaeee41159d89b8a5e32a6f9a4d492f6a6c","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BkIqod5ll","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"913a9263ce416ad81065b72d51e473134aa4a786e1fa68739aaec76b1de70c65","request_identity_sha256":"82fe6993c185454e1c67